# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies the whole working tree
# into the build context — including data/, which is the ~9.7 GB corpus. That is
# how uscode-redesign-api came to be a 20.4 GB image for what is a few hundred
# megabytes of Python. It also matters for the deploy: ADR-0020 gives the box a
# 20 GB root volume, which a 20 GB image does not fit in.
#
# The corpus reaches the container through a mounted volume
# (docker-compose.prod.yml maps ${DATA_ROOT}/releases), never through the image.

# The corpus. Never in an image — it comes from the S3 mirror (ADR-0013).
data/

# The RP samples: 32 MB of USLM that only the test suite reads.
samples/
tests/fixtures/

# Host build artefacts. The image builds its own (uv sync into /opt/venv,
# npm ci in the frontend stage), and copying these in both bloats the image and
# risks a host-architecture venv shadowing the container's.
.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.astro/
__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# History and local state.
.git/
.github/
.ci-data/
docs/screenshots/

# Secrets must not be baked into a layer. The compose files pass real values as
# environment variables at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
